  "description": "Retrospective application for refurbishment works to a block of flats. The works include replacement of the existing roof with a Garland roofing system incorporating upgraded insulation; replacement of rotten timber shiplap boarding with white uPVC shiplap boards to match the existing size and profile; replacement of existing single-glazed aluminium windows with uPVC windows to match the existing size, colour and profiles; and refurbishment of rear elevation balconies including replacement of defective decking and paving slabs with a Dura-Coat Restoration Waterproofing System with a uniform coloured finish. No change of use is proposed.\n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [01, 02, Heritage Statement, Fire Statement, Unnumbered location plan received 07/04/2026].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission."
